================================================================================
    SECTION 1: UNDERSTANDING PROP FIRM TRADING
================================================================================

Proprietary trading firms provide capital to traders who demonstrate consistent
profitability. As a funded trader, you trade the firm's money in exchange for a
profit split, typically ranging from 70% to 90% in your favor.

The evaluation process usually involves two phases. In Phase 1, you must hit a
profit target (commonly 8-10%) while staying within a maximum drawdown limit.
Phase 2 requires a smaller profit target (4-5%) with the same drawdown rules.

Key prop firm models include:
- Challenge-based firms (FTMO, MyFundedFX, The Funded Trader)
- Instant funding programs with higher profit splits to the firm
- Combine-style evaluations with live market simulations

The most important mindset shift: you are not trying to get rich on one account.
You are proving you can manage risk. Firms want consistency, not home runs.

================================================================================
    SECTION 2: RISK RULES AND ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

Every prop firm enforces strict risk parameters. Violating any single rule
results in immediate account termination with no exceptions.

DAILY DRAWDOWN RULE: Most firms cap daily losses at 4-5% of your starting
balance. This resets each trading day. If your account starts the day at
$100,000, you cannot lose more than $5,000 in that session. Calculate your
maximum position size BEFORE entering any trade.

MAXIMUM DRAWDOWN RULE: The trailing or static max drawdown is typically 8-12%.
A trailing drawdown moves up with your equity high-water mark, meaning profits
do not create a safety cushion. A static drawdown is measured from your initial
balance, which is more forgiving.

Position sizing formula for prop accounts:
    Risk per trade = 0.5% to 1% of account balance
    Stop loss distance determines lot size
    Example: $100K account, 1% risk = $1,000 max loss per trade
    If stop loss is 20 pips on EUR/USD, max lot size = 0.50 lots

CONSISTENCY RULES: Some firms require that no single trading day accounts for
more than 30-40% of your total profits. This prevents luck-based passes and
encourages steady, repeatable performance.

Never risk more than 1% on any single trade in a prop account. The math is
clear: even five consecutive losers only cost you 5%, well within drawdown
limits. But two 4% losers and you are done.

================================================================================
    SECTION 3: DEVELOPING A FUNDED ACCOUNT STRATEGY
================================================================================

The ideal prop firm strategy prioritizes capital preservation above all else.
Here is a framework that has passed thousands of evaluations:

TRADE SELECTION: Focus on 2-3 pairs or instruments maximum. Specialization
reduces decision fatigue and improves pattern recognition. Recommended pairs
for forex prop accounts include EUR/USD, GBP/USD, and USD/JPY due to their
liquidity and tighter spreads.

SESSION TIMING: Trade during the London-New York overlap (8:00-12:00 EST) for
maximum volatility and liquidity. Avoid trading during major news releases
unless your strategy specifically accounts for high-impact events.

ENTRY CRITERIA (must meet all three):
    1. Higher timeframe trend alignment (4H or Daily bias)
    2. Key level reaction (support/resistance, supply/demand zone)
    3. Lower timeframe entry trigger (engulfing candle, break of structure)

TRADE MANAGEMENT: Once a trade moves 1:1 risk-to-reward in your favor, move
your stop loss to break even. Target a minimum 1:2 risk-to-reward ratio. Take
partials at 1:1 and let the remainder run to 2:1 or beyond.

================================================================================
    SECTION 4: SCALING YOUR FUNDED CAREER
================================================================================

Once you pass your first evaluation, the real work begins. Treat every funded
account as a business asset generating monthly income.

MULTI-ACCOUNT STRATEGY: Run 2-4 funded accounts simultaneously across different
firms. This diversifies your income streams and protects against any single
firm's payout issues. Use the same strategy across all accounts for consistency.

SCALING PLAN:
    Month 1-3: Trade one $50K-$100K account, focus on consistency
    Month 4-6: Add a second account, increase to $200K total
    Month 7-12: Scale to $400K-$500K across multiple firms
    Year 2+: Manage $1M+ in funded capital with refined systems

PAYOUT MANAGEMENT: Most firms offer bi-weekly or monthly payouts. Withdraw
consistently rather than compounding. Your funded capital is not your money;
treat payouts as your actual trading income.

RECORD KEEPING: Maintain a detailed trading journal for every funded account.
Track your win rate, average risk-to-reward, maximum consecutive losses, and
profit factor. These metrics reveal whether your edge is sustainable.

The prop firm model has democratized access to institutional capital. Traders
who master risk management and maintain discipline can build a six-figure
income without risking personal savings.

